+ * guest address space above the RAM mirrors, fresh pages (no alias of low
+ * memory), mapped at layout time while the host range is still free. Only a
+ * request that would otherwise fail ever lands here, so nothing that works
+ * changes. Blocks are pages, first fit, merged when freed; the heap's own
+ * lock covers them. Off while RECOMP_EXT_VMA's tracker owns that range. */
